A||||6||87ECO5||Compatible Steering Columns?||||1||
Z||000000||87ECO5||04-19-2000||08:59 AM||||The column in my '87 coupe has the "wobble" problem so I've been looking at replacing it.  I've got an '84 parts car with a solid column.  Both cars have manual transmissions, both columns have the tilt option and delay wipers.  However, the '84 had cruise, my '87 does not.<P>Can/will the column from the '84 work in the '87?<P>TIA||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||04-19-2000||09:06 AM||||should. just change the lolly pop to the one for 87.||||reg||1
Z||000002||87ECO5||04-19-2000||09:44 AM||||Sorry, Ogre.  Do you mean the stalk?  If so, is it a "plug and play" swap (replace the old stalk with the new stalk without any wiring mods)?||||reg||1
Z||000003||DaveT||04-19-2000||10:02 AM||||The two levers are interchangeable.Just the lever with cruise will have a wire for the cruise button.Just push the lever in,turn it<BR>and it will come out,undo wire and the other lever is plug and play!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||N_Man||04-19-2000||12:23 PM||||on a similar note I can get a steering column for dirt cheep but it has no ignition key.  Sooo can i switch the ignition locks or do I need to get a new key cut?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Patrick||04-19-2000||01:42 PM||||<BR>I don't know if it's possible to get a new key cut if you don't have some way of establishing what you need. The ignition locks are certainly swapable. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||04-19-2000||07:58 PM||||Yes. you can change the lock.<P>you need the wheel and lock plate off. then take out the screws that hold the turn signal selector.(remove the hazard button. It has 2 phillips screw in the center.)<P>then there is a wire held under the lock by a clip. Carefully pull it out. One screw holds the lock in.<P>time consuming. not hard.||||reg||1
